I have ascended with a Ki-rin mount before, so I can give you a little
advice.

1) Hitting with a wielded potion has the expected effect with all
healing potions, speed, invisibility, sickness, blindness, and
paralysis, but others will not have the expected effect, IIRC.

2) Yes, Ki-rin will pick up and drink useful potions.  But if you want
a pet to pick up and use useful items, you need to give it no choices
- trap it at the end of a narrow corridor standing on top of the items
you want it to pick up and use, with the items in a pile at its feet.
If it cannot move, it is likely to pick something up pretty quickly,
and if it is a useful item, it will probably use it instead of
dropping it.

What items are essential for a Ki-rin pet? I equip my ki-rin with the
following:
A blessed saddle (the ki-rin can't use that itself, so you need to
apply it onto the pet)
an amulet of lifesaving
a highly enchanted shield of reflection.
highly enchanted boots, gloves and helmet
a blessed unicorn horn

Keep spare amulets of lifesaving to give to your ki-rin if it uses up
the one it is wearing.  Use a wand of probing to check its inventory
and status.

If you are planning on leveling up your ki-rin, note that at a high
enough level it will become immune to your magic, so you would be
unable to re-tame it if it goes wild unless you level-drain it.

